                <pb facs="0511" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890G.00/576: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-04-22T18:00:00-05:00">April 22, 1941—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. Your 89, April 19, 3 p.m. The Department agrees that a written communication
                    to the Foreign Minister is unnecessary at this time. However, there is no
                    objection to your establishing informal contact without instructions on the
                    question of official recognition.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
